    49|      "body": "Hi {{name}},\n\nEvery book has a story behind it — and No Blue Sky is no exception.\n\nI didn't set out to write a five-volume science fiction series. It started with a single image that wouldn't leave my head: a person standing on an alien world, looking up at a sky that wasn't blue, feeling utterly alone yet strangely at peace.\n\nThat image became Ignition. And once I started writing, the story took on a life of its own. Characters appeared fully formed. Worlds built themselves. What I thought would be a single book became a sprawling saga about courage, identity, and the choices that define us when everything familiar is gone.\n\nI wrote most of No Blue Sky early in the morning, before the day job started. Some chapters were rewritten a dozen times. Others poured out in one sitting, as if they'd been waiting for me to catch up.\n\nTomorrow is Still Open came from a different place entirely — quieter, more personal. It's the book I needed to write when I was figuring out how to start over.\n\n🎁 I'd love to share that experience with you. Reply to this email with the word \"SAMPLE\" and I'll send you a free sample chapter from any book of your choice — no strings attached.\n\nWant to know what happens in the first chapter of Ignition? Curious about the opening of Tomorrow is Still Open? Just say the word.\n\nMore soon,\nBob Mills\n\nP.S. — On Day 7, I'll share what early readers and reviewers have been saying. Spoiler: some of it surprised even me.",
